<InteriorLayout title="Website Privacy | I.S Design + Build" description="How the current I.S Design + Build website handles project enquiry information." label="Privacy policy" headline="Your information. A clear explanation.">
  <Fragment slot="intro"><p>This notice describes the contact features currently available on this website.</p></Fragment>
  <section class="copy-section"><p class="cg-label">Website enquiries</p><div class="copy-body"><h2>Preparing an email</h2><p>The project enquiry tool prepares text in your browser. It does not send the details to a website form service or save them in a company database. Choosing “Open my email app” passes the prepared text to your email application. You decide whether to send it.</p><p>A page reload or closing the page may clear the information you entered. You can copy the text yourself before leaving the page.</p><h2>Contacting the company</h2><p>If you email or call us, the information you share is used to respond to your question and discuss your project. Please share only information needed for that enquiry. A town or ZIP code is sufficient to begin discussing coverage.</p><h2>Website hosting and external links</h2><p>This site is hosted by Vercel, which processes technical request information to deliver and protect the website. Links to Google reviews and other external services take you to sites with their own privacy practices. Your email provider also processes messages sent through your email app.</p><h2>Website analytics</h2><p>This site uses Google Analytics to understand how visitors find and use it, such as which pages are viewed and the general location and type of device. Google processes this information and may use cookies or similar identifiers. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p><h2>Questions about your information</h2><p>Contact <a href="mailto:info@isdesignandbuild.com">info@isdesignandbuild.com</a> to ask about information you have shared or request its correction or deletion. Any future online submission or AI features will need an updated notice describing their data handling before they are introduced.</p></div></section>
</InteriorLayout>
